# Medicine AI System

An AI-powered medicine identification and drug interaction checking platform. Users can upload an image of a pill to identify it and verify potential drug-drug interactions among their medications.

## Features
- Pill image upload & preprocessing
- (Placeholder) Pill identification model inference
- Medication catalog & sample interaction checking
- REST-style Flask routes with HTML templates
- Modular architecture for future expansion (training, retraining, evaluation)

## Project Structure
```
medicine_ai_system/
  src/
    app.py                # Flask app factory and routes
    models/               # ML + ORM models
    utils/                # Helpers: image processing, interactions, database
    templates/            # Jinja2 HTML templates
    static/               # CSS/JS/Images
  data/                   # Raw & processed image data
  models/trained_models/  # Persisted model artifacts
  tests/                  # Pytest test suite
```

## Quick Start
```powershell
# (Recommended) Create virtual environment
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Run dev server
python run.py

# Visit http://localhost:5000
```

## Training Example
```powershell
python train_model.py --epochs 10 --output pill_mobilenetv2.keras
```

## Configuration
Environment determined by `FLASK_ENV` and settings in `config.py`. Override values using environment variables:
- `DATABASE_URL`
- `SECRET_KEY`

## Testing
```powershell
pytest -q
```

## Notes
- Dataset structure example (place images under each class):
```
data/pills_dataset/
  aspirin/ img1.jpg ...
  ibuprofen/ img2.jpg ...
  acetaminophen/ ...
  metformin/ ...
```

- The training script performs a stratified split into train/val/test and saves:
  - `models/trained_models/pill_mobilenetv2.keras`
  - `models/trained_models/pill_mobilenetv2_labels.json`

- Replace placeholder logic in `image_processing.py` as needed. The Flask route will automatically use the trained model if present.

